-- title:
--   Mumford glue datum exists for a type-preserving Schottky group
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ assumed to be a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi \in \mathcal O$ whose residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and a field $K_0$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra realising the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ have underlying matrix $\operatorname{diag}(\pi,1)$, and let $N \le \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be a subgroup which acts on the Bruhat–Tits tree `BruhatTits.tree` $\mathcal O\,K_0$ (vertices: full $\mathcal O$-lattices in $K_0^2$ up to the equivalence implicit in `Vertex`, edges generated by the adjacency relation `AdjacentLattice`) in a Schottky way, that is: every vertex stabiliser in $N$ is trivial, no element of $N$ carries a dart to its reverse, and $N$ has only finitely many orbits of vertices and of darts; moreover $N$ is contained in `typePreserving`, the subgroup of elements $g$ with $\operatorname{dist}(v_0, g\cdot w) \equiv \operatorname{dist}(v_0,w) \pmod 2$ for all vertices $w$, where $v_0$ is the class of the standard lattice. The conclusion is that the type `MumfordGlue` $\mathcal O\,\pi\,K_0\,r\,g_1\,N$ is nonempty: there is a datum consisting of schemes $Z_n$ ($n \in \mathbb N$) with structure morphisms $z^{\mathrm b}_n : Z_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ that are flat and separated, transition morphisms $z^{\mathrm t}_n : Z_n \to Z_{n+1}$ exhibiting $Z_n$ as the fibre product of $Z_{n+1}$ with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2})$, and charts $\zeta_{h,n} : \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(E/\pi^{n+1}\bigr) \to Z_n$ indexed by $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, where $E =$ `chartERing` $\mathcal O\,\pi\,r$ is the localisation of the edge chart ring away from `edgeQuot.discr`; the charts are open immersions, lie over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, are compatible with the $z^{\mathrm t}_n$ via reduction on $E$, satisfy $\zeta_{gh,n} = \zeta_{h,n}$ whenever the class of $g$ lies in $N$, and for each $n$ finitely many of them cover $Z_n$; finally the datum carries the fields `ζ_rel`, `ζ_overlap_local`, `ζ_overlap_zar` and `ζ_univ`, the first describing the points of the charts in terms of `DeligneDatum`s whose lines on the standard lattice and on its $g_1$-translate are spanned by the vectors built from the chart coordinates `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η`, the next two governing the overlaps of chart images, and the last a universal property of the family of charts.
--
--   This is the existence statement for Mumford's gluing construction in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting: from a type-preserving Schottky subgroup of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ one manufactures the formal-scheme levels $Z_n$ over $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ together with the family of edge charts indexed by $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and invariant under $N$. It feeds the construction of the Mumford tower, [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordTower_of_isSchottky`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordTower_of_isSchottky).
